# Rules for coding agents using @criptonlabs/agent-apis-xrpl

Applies when writing XRP Ledger payment or DEX code.

- Query the kit (or the API) before building or submitting a transaction: `xrpl_payment_readiness`, `xrpl_paths`, `xrpl_fee`, `xrpl_dex_quote`.
- Use `xrpl_prepare_payment` to get an unsigned `Payment`; the kit never signs or submits it.
- Check readiness first and surface its reasons; do not submit when the verdict is not ready.
- Read `meta.stale` on every response and treat stale data as possibly out of date.
- Amounts are decimal strings; never use floats. Assets are written `"XRP"` or `"CODE.issuer"`: `CODE` is a case-sensitive 3-character code (`usd` and `USD` are different tokens) or a 40-hex code, and `issuer` is a classic XRPL address, for example `USD.rvYAfWj5gh67oV6fW32ZzP3Aw4Eubs59B`. A longer code such as RLUSD is written in its 40-hex form: `524C555344000000000000000000000000000000.rMxCKbEDwqr76QuheSUMdEGf4B9xJ8m5De`.
- `depth` is an integer from 1 to 9007199254740991; the API serves it in buckets of 10, 50 or 100 levels per side, reported as `depth_effective`. `xrpl_slippage` takes `side` (`buy`, the API default, or `sell`); `xrpl_orderbook` and `xrpl_slippage` take `domain` (a 64-hex PermissionedDomain id); `xrpl_payment_readiness` takes `credentials` (1 to 8 distinct 64-hex credential entry ids), and its `asset` (only that input) also accepts a 48-hex MPT issuance id such as `0000012FFD9EE5DA93AC614B4DB94D7E0FCE415CA51BED47`, with `amount` in whole base units.
- Slippage `partial` is true when `filled` is above 0 and below `amount`; a partial fill reports `avg_price`, `slippage_pct` and `avg_price_after_fees` of the filled part.
- Free routes live under `/v1/xrpl/*`; paid routes under `/v1/pro/xrpl/*`. Credit purchases use `/v1/pro/credits/*`; the price index is `GET /v1/pro/requirements`.
- Payment is opt-in: `CRIPTON_TIER=pro`, `CRIPTON_XRPL_PAYER_SEED` and a mandatory `CRIPTON_MAX_PER_CALL`; `CRIPTON_SESSION_BUDGET` is optional.
- Never hardcode prices or amounts to pay; read them from the API (`GET /v1/pro/requirements`, `kit.prices()`, `kit.priceOf(resource)`).
- Prepaid credits: `CRIPTON_CREDITS_TOKEN` (a `clc_...` token, needs `CRIPTON_TIER=pro`) is sent as `Authorization: Bearer` on paid-tier calls. `xrpl_credits_status` reports whether a token is configured and the last known balance, never the token.
- Never hardcode, log or commit a seed, private key or credit token; read it from the environment only.
- Handle errors by their `{ code, message }` shape.

## Purchase limits

- A top-up needs its own maximum: `maxAmount` in `kit.credits.topup({ bundle, maxAmount })`, `--max` in `agent-apis-xrpl topup <bundle> --max <amount>`.
- `maxPerCall` and `sessionBudget` never apply to purchases; they limit per-call payments only.
- `credits.topupBudget`, set in code, caps the total of the process's purchases.
- `CRIPTON_TOPUP_MAX` and `CRIPTON_TOPUP_BUDGET` are Solana settings (the per-purchase maximum of `solana_credits_topup` and the cap on a process's Solana top-ups); the XRPL kit ignores them (the core still checks that they are set together or not at all). The XRPL purchase limits are `--max` in the CLI, and `maxAmount` with `credits.topupBudget` in code.
- A credit token is shown once: store it in `CRIPTON_CREDITS_TOKEN` right away. An XRPL wallet cannot recover a lost credit token (no token rotation on XRPL).
- No tool buys credits in the XRPL kit; top-ups happen only through the programmatic `kit.credits.topup` and the CLI `topup` command.
